From 72ee6e954aa60343329d55e2d35354165366375e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:37:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Node machine: the tests where they sit, at reader time, in
 the shadow

Part of #2524. What decides which expressions the machine may take
stayed after the pipeline: the census's set and its silence tests, which
read the stream. measure-node-machine --shadow --front-tests runs them
at reader time: after T takes an expression and before C and X, the
census's own test code on T's records. After the pipeline the census's
verdict for the same root is compared with it, test by test, on the
roots the lowering pops and (read again from the stream) on those it
never pops. An expression reader time takes that the census refuses, a
test's bit or a root's kind that differs, fails the command.

The tests read a node through a view (node_view_value and its kin): the
stream's after the pipeline, T's record at reader time. What else they
read has a stand-in before the pipeline: the root's kind is the front's
root's operator (a nested control's inside a statement expression), an
initializer's object's type the declaration's, the enabled warnings the
unit's policy, a pragma's body the outermost braces around it, the
events the reader's own so far, an action's warnings T's own for the
expression (NodeMachine.action_warnings), a packed member's address any
address in a unit with a packed record. A body that tracks its stack
and a node popped twice are the lowering's, a splice's to read.

A declaration's discard is no root any more: at a declaration's `;` the
walk casts each initializer's value to void, the front made that cast a
root, and nothing evaluates it. Reader time leaves it alone, by the
parser's tree (node_machine_reader_discard).

The census's own code: a byte a type and a byte a declaration keep what
the tests ask of each, the constants', the tree's and the truth's tests
are asked only where a node's operator can fail them, and
-Wassign-enum is read from the unit's policy. Its reports are the same.
T keeps a conditional's third operand's conversion; --verify at reader
time counts the nodes a row or a rule typed whose action warns.
PPOptions.node_reader is a byte beside node_front, whose bits are taken.

No compile takes it. test-checker: the six census fixtures run with the
tests at reader time (exact counts of refused expressions and of
discards, a record with its test's bit at each silence line), with new
lines for a conditional's third conversion, an argument's conversion, a
member's offset and a diagnostic pragma's body.

